      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the structure. The key improvements are:\n1. Remove ~15 unused data provider methods and all unused imports\n2. Format `data_plus()` rows one-per-line with alignment\n3. Rename cryptic parameters (`expectedYear...dom`) to (`expectedYear/Month/Day` and `startYear/Month/Day`) to make the minus semantics clear\n4. Add a concise column-header comment\n\nLet me write the improved test file.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused data provider methods and imports, formats `data_plus()` one row per line with alignment and unit-based grouping, renames parameters from cryptic `expectedYear/dom/year` to self-describing `expectedYear/Month/Day` and `startYear/Month/Day`, and adds a concise column-header comment — all without changing the test's runtime behaviour."
